      "id": "can-receive-property-bag-details-drop-on-graph-pin",
      "name": "CanReceivePropertyBagDetailsDropOnGraphPin",
      "category": "IPropertyBagEditorGraph",
      "signature": "CanReceivePropertyBagDetailsDropOnGraphPin(Target, Pin)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "IPropertyBagEdGraphDragAndDrop*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Pin",
          "type": "UEdGraphPin*"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "Bool",
      "docs": "PropertyBag Editor Drag and Drop public interface.\nUsage: This interface can be used independently or as a part of the IPropertyBagEdGraph interface (below), to be\ninherited by custom subclasses of UEdGraph. Once inherited, implement the following member overrides to validate and\nreceive Drag and Drop operations from a PropertyBag details child row. The PropertyBagDragDropHandler\n(see PropertyBagDragDropHandler.h/.cpp) inherits from FGraphEditorDragDropAction, mimicking a graph schema action\nbeing dropped into the graph, or onto a pin or node.\nNote: The base handler class currently climbs down ownership from Graph->Pin, so if only the graph is valid, it will\nattempt the graph panel drop through the pins' or nodes' parent graph."
    },
